<Page title="Privacy — VAIS Boundary" description="How the VAIS Boundary website handles contact messages."><section class="wrap page-content prose"><p class="eyebrow">VAIS Boundary</p><h1>Privacy.</h1><h2>Contact messages</h2><p>The contact form asks for your name, email address, and message so the project maintainer can respond. Please do not include passwords, API keys, or other confidential information.</p><p>Messages are processed by Web3Forms and delivered to the maintainer’s email inbox. The form uses hCaptcha to help prevent spam. These providers process data under their own policies: <a href="https://web3forms.com/privacy">Web3Forms privacy policy</a> and <a href="https://www.hcaptcha.com/privacy">hCaptcha privacy policy</a>.</p><h2>Website hosting</h2><p>This website is hosted by GitHub Pages. GitHub may process connection information such as IP addresses to operate and secure its service. See the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub privacy statement</a>.</p><h2>Analytics and requests</h2><p>This website does not add advertising or analytics trackers. To ask about a message you have sent or request its deletion from the maintainer’s inbox, use the contact form.</p></section></Page>
